Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:05.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}First track: fast surrogates,\Nnetworks trained to imitate a solver.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.12,0:00:11.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Some carry the equations in their loss;\Nothers learn maps between whole fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.89,0:00:16.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}For conducting fluids, they now reach\Nflat, two-dimensional turbulence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.04,0:00:20.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}For the Earth, recall the\Ntwenty twenty-two study:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.33,0:00:24.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}the methods it tried could\Nnot reliably foresee a flip.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.03,0:00:28.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Their weak spot: trained to\Nminimize a mean-square error,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.88,0:00:32.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}ensembles of them\Nregress to the mean flow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.36,0:00:35.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A cloud with two polarities\Ncollapses to its middle.
